## Project Architecture

- **Product**: B-LAN
- **Shape**: Flutter app. Local folder share, mDNS peer discovery, pinned HTTPS chunk transfers. Nearby proximity (BLE + private network) is a planned layer on top of the same transfer stack.
- **Platforms**: Linux, macOS, Windows, Android, limited web. iOS platform code and expected tests are in scope for proximity; assert against mocks until a Mac can run them.
- **Primary language**: Dart 3.13 / Flutter 3.47 (stable channel on this machine)
- **Build / verify**: `make verify` (`flutter analyze`, `flutter test`, `flutter build apk --debug`)

```
lib/
  app/            shell, providers
  core/
    discovery/    mDNS advertise + browse
    indexing/     scan, hash, watch
    network/      pinned HTTP client
    persistence/  Drift
    protocol/     DTOs, ports
    security/     Ed25519, TLS, secrets, sessions
    transfers/    shelf HTTPS server + download client
  features/       shares, peers, browse, search, transfers, settings
  platform/       Android / desktop / stub services
android/          manifest, foreground service
```

LAN sharing is already implemented: `_blan._tcp`, TXT `peerId` / `pv` / `nick` / `tls` / `scheme`, HTTPS `:59488`, browser HTTP `:59487` on loopback. Trust is explicit and persistent. Untrusted peer rows are purged on next launch. Browse works before trust. An untrusted download asks once vs trust.

Nearby proximity does not replace that path. It adds a BLE list and, when the peer is not reachable on the current LAN, a private network whose address is then used by the existing client.

### Inspiration sources

- D-LAN (C++ predecessor): folder share on a LAN
- Quick Share: nearby list, one accept dialog, then a high-speed local link
- SecureSettingsManager `ShizukuManager`: provider detection for Shevery and Shizuku

### Build & Run

```bash
flutter pub get
dart run build_runner build   # after Drift table edits
make verify                    # analyze + test + android debug apk
make install-hooks             # once per clone; pre-commit runs make quick-verify (analyze+test)
flutter run -d linux
```

